  "narrative": {
    "intro": "McKesson has $12.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. McKesson has 2,348 awards in the current fiscal year to date and an average award size of $5.2M. McKesson's obligations are up 3.7% year over year. McKesson's federal work is concentrated in Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing, which accounts for $12.3B of obligations in FY2026 to date. McKesson's largest federal buyer is the Department of Veterans Affairs, which obligated $12B in FY2026 to date. McKesson's other top buyers include the Department of Justice at $194M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $86.5M, while the Department of State shows $0. McKesson's obligations rose from $7.7B in FY21 to $12.3B in FY26 to date, with a dip to $9B in FY24 and recovery to $11.9B in FY25. McKesson's NAICS breakdown also lists smaller dollar entries, including positive and negative adjustments in specific merchant wholesaler and manufacturing categories.",
